//? Title: Test goodness of fit with empirical distribution functions
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en

> Choose the Anderson–Darling reference

The first sample contains fractions to compare with a uniform distribution
on [0, 1]. Because that distribution is fixed in advance, simulated uniform
probabilities give the reference. The second sample contains measurements
on an unknown normal scale. Its reference fits the mean and sample standard
deviation anew in every simulated normal sample.

```{cpp, id=anderson-darling-references, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <datamunge/stats/edf_tests.hpp>
#include <print>

int main() {
    using namespace datamunge::stats;
    const std::vector<double> fractions{.05, .11, .12, .19, .22, .44, .46, .61, .86};
    const std::vector<double> measurements{-3.2, -1.1, -.6, -.15, 0, .1, .4, 1.4, 4.7};
    datamunge::random::SplitMix64 rng(73);
    const auto specified = anderson_darling_test(fractions, [](double x) { return x; }, 4095, rng);
    const auto fitted = anderson_darling_normal_test(measurements, 4095, rng);
    std::println("| Reference | Anderson–Darling statistic | Simulated p-value |");
    std::println("| --- | ---: | ---: |");
    std::println("| Specified uniform | {:.3f} | {:.3f} |", specified.statistic, specified.p_value);
    std::println("| Fitted normal | {:.3f} | {:.3f} |", fitted.statistic, fitted.p_value);
    std::println("");
    std::println("The fitted normal mean is {:.3f} and its sample standard deviation is {:.3f}.",
                 fitted.estimate1, fitted.estimate2);
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
| Reference | Anderson–Darling statistic | Simulated p-value |
| --- | ---: | ---: |
| Specified uniform | 1.594 | 0.158 |
| Fitted normal | 0.520 | 0.142 |

The fitted normal mean is 0.172 and its sample standard deviation is 2.115.
// result_end

> Compare squared CDF differences with Cramér–von Mises

Cramér–von Mises integrates squared CDF differences. The one-sample
test compares the fractions with the specified uniform distribution.
The two-sample test compares independent groups at the pooled observed
values, with each tied value weighted by its multiplicity. For these small
groups the program enumerates all 35 assignments at the observed sizes.

```{cpp, id=cramer-von-mises-references, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <datamunge/stats/edf_tests.hpp>
#include <print>

int main() {
    using namespace datamunge::stats;
    const std::vector<double> fractions{.05, .11, .12, .19, .22, .44, .46, .61, .86};
    datamunge::random::SplitMix64 rng(73);
    const auto specified = cramer_von_mises_test(fractions, [](double x) { return x; }, 4095, rng);
    const auto pooled = cramer_von_mises_test_two_sample_exact({0, 1, 1}, {1, 2, 2, 4});
    std::println("| Reference | Cramér–von Mises statistic | p-value |");
    std::println("| --- | ---: | ---: |");
    std::println("| Simulated specified uniform | {:.3f} | {:.3f} |", specified.statistic, specified.p_value);
    std::println("| Exact pooled labels | {:.3f} | {:.3f} |", pooled.statistic, pooled.p_value);
    std::println("");
    std::println("{:.0f} of the {:.0f} pooled assignments have statistics at least as large as observed.",
                 pooled.parameter2, pooled.parameter1);
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
| Reference | Cramér–von Mises statistic | p-value |
| --- | ---: | ---: |
| Simulated specified uniform | 0.310 | 0.119 |
| Exact pooled labels | 0.471 | 0.114 |

4 of the 35 pooled assignments have statistics at least as large as observed.
// result_end

> Compare three samples with tied values

Three independent groups record scores on an integer scale. At a tied
score, the midrank statistic uses the midpoint of each empirical CDF
jump. Under the common-distribution null, the seven observations can
be reassigned to groups of sizes three, two, and two. Both references
keep those sizes fixed.

```{cpp, id=midrank-multisample-reference, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <datamunge/stats/edf_tests.hpp>
#include <print>

int main() {
    using namespace datamunge::stats;
    const std::vector<std::vector<double>> groups{{0, 1, 1}, {1, 2}, {2, 3}};
    const auto exact = anderson_darling_k_sample_test_exact(groups);
    datamunge::random::SplitMix64 rng(7);
    const auto sampled = anderson_darling_k_sample_test(groups, 4095, rng);
    std::println("The observed midrank statistic is {:.3f}.", exact.statistic);
    std::println("");
    std::println("| Reference | Assignments | Upper-tail assignments | p-value |");
    std::println("| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |");
    for (const auto& [label, result] : {std::pair{"Exact", exact}, std::pair{"Simulated", sampled}}) {
        std::println("| {} | {:.0f} | {:.0f} | {:.3f} |",
                     label, result.parameter1, result.parameter2, result.p_value);
    }
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
The observed midrank statistic is 3.497.

| Reference | Assignments | Upper-tail assignments | p-value |
| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| Exact | 210 | 30 | 0.143 |
| Simulated | 4095 | 582 | 0.142 |
// result_end

